      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Answer HR policy questions in Telegram with RAG (Groq, Gemini embeddings, Google Drive)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow builds a retrieval-augmented HR policy assistant for Telegram. A manual ingestion path downloads an HR policy PDF from Google Drive, parses it, creates Gemini embeddings, and inserts the content into an in-memory vector store. When a Telegram message arrives, an AI agent uses Groq, chat memory, and the policy vector store to answer the employee\u2019s question, then sends the response back to Telegram.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Google Drive credentials and point the download node to the HR policy PDF file.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for both embedding nodes used during insert and retrieval.\n- Configure Groq credentials for the chat model used by the HR Policy Agent.\n- Configure Telegram bot credentials for the trigger and reply nodes, including the correct chat/message fields.\n- Run the manual knowledge-base loading path before answering questions so the in-memory vector store is populated.\n\n### Customization\n\nSwap the Google Drive file for another policy document, adjust the agent prompt and Groq model, tune PDF loading/chunking behavior, or replace the in-memory vector store with a persistent vector database if the index must survive workflow restarts."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ca9085bb-90c8-4f37-8ed3-eb574e577e50",
